In some cases, the nature of the duty owed may exculpate the plaintiff from a claim of con- tributory negligence; in other cases, the nature of the duty may reduce the plaintiffs share of responsibility for the damage suffered;
and in yet other cases the nature of the duty may not prevent a finding that the plaintiff failed to take reasonable care for the safety of his or her person or MACT No.
